 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per pixel for the normalization division step.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(H \times W)$ for the depth and opacity buffers.
-*   **Strengths:** Produces geometrically accurate depth maps in transparent or semi-transparent regions where standard depth accumulation fails [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Sensitive to noise in low-opacity regions due to division by small values; requires robust handling of zero-opacity pixels [G].
-*   **When to use:** When accurate depth estimation is needed for scenes with varying opacity [G].
-*   **When not to use:** When simple geometric depth is sufficient and opacity is uniform, or when performance constraints prohibit the extra division step [G].
